# API documentation updates required

Any backend change that affects the HTTP API must update `API_DOCUMENTATION.md` in the same change.

## Triggers

- New, removed, or renamed routes in `internal/application/app.go`
- Changed request/response bodies, status codes, or error codes
- Changed auth (public / authenticated / admin)
- CORS or other client-visible HTTP behavior

## Checklist

1. Update the endpoint index if routes changed
2. Update the endpoint section (path, method, body, response)
3. Keep examples matching the real `{ status, data, error }` envelope
4. Do not document routes that are not registered in `SetupRoutes`

Route source of truth: `internal/application/app.go`.
